[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +Previously the cursor only stored ``created_at``.  When multiple orders share
[?2004l[?2004h> +the same timestamp (common because timestamps are second‑resolution) the next
[?2004l[?2004h> +page used ``created_at < ?`` and inadvertently skipped the remaining rows with
[?2004l[?2004h> +that timestamp.  This caused missing orders during exports and API walks.
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +The fix stores **both** ``created_at`` and ``id`` in the cursor and updates the
[?2004l[?2004h> +SQL to respect the full ordering, eliminating the gap.
